INSERT INTO `sales_leads` VALUES (1,'Sonia Ben Ali','Softylines',NULL,'HR Director','autopilot_discovery','qualified',85,'Strategy: Connect on LinkedIn with Sonia Ben Ali, reference Softylines\' recent growth, then send a tailored email highlighting a Tunisian SaaS case study where Candway cut senior‑dev time‑to‑hire from 45 to 12 days while improving cultural‑fit scores. Offer a free 2‑week pilot for senior developer and account‑executive roles, schedule a short demo call to show real‑time skill and cultural‑fit scoring, and follow with a value‑based proposal aligned to their hiring volume. Continue nurturing with industry insights and a regional AI‑recruitment round‑table.\nPain Point: The need to quickly source senior developers and account executives who not only have the required expertise but also fit Softylines\' culture, enabling fast, reliable scaling of their engineering and sales teams.\nContext: Softylines (Sousse) delivers a subscription‑based invoicing & accounting SaaS used by SMEs across Tunisia. The team has grown to ~100 employees in the last 12 months and is opening multiple engineering and sales positions. AI‑recruitment would help them quickly identify senior developers and account‑executives while maintaining a high cultural fit.','2026-08-26 09:25:06','2026-08-26 09:25:06',NULL),(2,'Karim Trabelsi','Weecover',NULL,'Chief Talent Officer','autopilot_discovery','new',50,'Strategy: Standard Pitch\nPain Point: Inefficient screening\nContext: Weecover (Lac II) is an insur‑tech SaaS platform that provides APIs for embedded insurance. After closing a €2 M seed round in early 2024, the company is expanding its product team from 5 to >20 engineers. An AI‑driven sourcing engine can surface niche talent (e.g., API‑design, fintech security) that the local market struggles to provide.','2026-08-26 09:25:11','2026-08-26 09:25:11',NULL),(3,'Meriem Chaâbane','nextav.ai',NULL,'HR Manager','autopilot_discovery','qualified',85,'Strategy: Email subject: “Speed‑up nextav.ai’s hiring for data‑science & GIS talent”. Email body: congratulate Meriem on the $1.5 M Series A, acknowledge the urgent need for data‑scientists, GIS engineers and sales specialists, explain how Candway’s AI‑driven platform cuts time‑to‑hire by 30‑40 % and boosts match quality, include a brief Tunisian SaaS case study, and propose a 15‑minute discovery call with a free Hiring Funnel Health Check. Follow‑up on day 2, day 7, and day 14 with a PDF, case‑study link, and a pilot offer.\nPain Point: Accelerating hiring cycles while ensuring high technical match quality for data‑scientists, GIS engineers, and sales specialists.\nContext: nextav.ai (Sousse) offers AI‑powered remote‑sensing SaaS for mining, agriculture and environmental monitoring. With a recent $1.5 M Series A and a headcount increase to 19, they need data‑scientists, GIS engineers and sales specialists. AI recruitment can accelerate hiring cycles and improve technical match quality.','2026-08-26 09:25:16','2026-08-26 09:25:16',NULL),(4,'Noureddine Gharbi','BUSINESS & AI',NULL,'Head of People & Culture','autopilot_discovery','qualified',85,'Strategy: Personalized outreach to Noureddine Gharbi: start with a warm LinkedIn/InMail referencing BUSINESS & AI\'s rapid growth and MENA expansion, highlight Candway\'s AI‑powered platform that cuts time‑to‑hire for rare AI‑finance roles by 30‑40%, attach a relevant case study, offer a 15‑minute demo showing live talent snapshots for senior AI engineers in the region, and follow up with a concise cadence (Day 1, Day 3, Day 7) while referencing a recent BUSINESS & AI press release for extra personalization.\nPain Point: Difficulty sourcing senior AI‑finance talent (AI engineers, product managers, compliance experts) across the MENA region; Candway solves this by providing a targeted, AI‑driven talent pool and efficient matching to dramatically shorten hiring cycles.\nContext: BUSINESS & AI (Tunis) builds AI‑enhanced SaaS tools for financial institutions. The firm doubled its staff in 2023 and is now targeting the broader MENA market, requiring senior AI engineers, product managers and compliance experts. AI‑recruitment will help them source candidates with rare AI‑finance skill‑sets across the region.','2026-08-26 09:25:21','2026-08-26 09:25:21',NULL),(5,'Leïla Ben Youssef','Cynoia',NULL,'Talent Acquisition Lead','autopilot_discovery','qualified',85,'Strategy: Research Hook: reference Cynoia’s 2024 growth round and team expansion. Value Proposition: AI matching cuts time‑to‑fill by ~40% for SaaS firms in Tunisia. Social Proof: share a local SaaS case‑study with 30% cost savings. Tailored Offer: 2‑week pilot on 2‑3 roles, success‑based fee. Call‑to‑Action: propose 15‑min discovery call (Tue 10am or Thu 2pm Sousse time). Channels: LinkedIn InMail + personalized email.\nPain Point: Lengthy, manual recruitment cycles that delay hiring for technical and commercial roles, slowing Cynoia’s scaling momentum.\nContext: Cynoia (Sousse) provides an all‑in‑one project‑management SaaS used by enterprises in North Africa. After raising a modest growth round in 2024, the company is scaling its sales, customer‑success and engineering teams (now ~35 people). AI‑driven candidate matching can reduce time‑to‑fill for both technical and commercial roles.','2026-08-26 09:25:35','2026-08-26 09:25:35',NULL),(6,'test-form-2','Candway Test','test-form-2@candway.tn',NULL,'demo_request','new',0,NULL,'2026-08-26 09:48:37','2026-08-26 09:48:37',NULL);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `sales_leads` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

